{
 "id": "78be94429d3e",
 "task": "When should we schedule maintenance on the charging stations in the Bolzano area to minimise impact on users? Propose concrete weekday/time windows backed by observed usage.",
 "preset": "maintenance",
 "engine": "claude",
 "model": "sonnet",
 "status": "ok",
 "started_at": "2026-11-14T06:49:59.618610+00:00",
 "markdown": "## Answer\nSchedule Bolzano-area maintenance on Tuesday, Thursday or Friday between 05:00 and 07:00 local time, with Thursday the best choice at 0.066 occupancy [E2]. Evenings between 20:00 and 23:00 on Monday, Wednesday and Saturday are the worst times, with Wednesday 20:00-22:00 at 0.72 [E2]. These windows rest on only 4 to 5 comparable dates each, so treat them as a well-supported but tentative choice [E2].\n\n## Key findings\n- Overall Bolzano occupancy is 0.435 (share of point-time occupied, not energy or demand) [E2].\n- The lowest-usage windows are Thu 05:00-07:00 at 0.066 (5 dates), Tue 05:00-07:00 at 0.124 (4 dates) and Fri 05:00-07:00 at 0.146 (4 dates) [E2].\n- The busiest windows are Wed 20:00-22:00 at 0.72 (6 dates), Sat 21:00-23:00 at 0.654 (5 dates) and Mon 20:00-22:00 at 0.651 (4 dates) [E2].\n- Weekday daytime occupancy runs from about 0.4 to 0.66 between 08:00 and 19:00, for example Thu 08:00 at 0.661 and Wed 08:00 at 0.636, so early morning is the clear trough [E2].\n- The busiest site, BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01, has occupancy 0.669, full-time share 0.462 and 203 observed starts, and has no quiet window: its lowest are Sat 19:00-21:00 at 0.449, Mon 15:00-17:00 at 0.465 and Fri 13:00-15:00 at 0.469 [E3, E4].\n- BZ_P_VITTORIA (occupancy 0.635, 135 starts) and BZ_BOEHLER_01 (occupancy 0.57, full-time 0.57, 170 starts) are also heavily used, so the Bolzano-wide quiet windows are not site-specific [E3].\n\n## Recommendation\n- Make Thu 05:00-07:00 the first-choice slot, with Tue 05:00-07:00 and Fri 05:00-07:00 as alternatives [E2].\n- Do not schedule work in the evening peaks: Wed 20:00-22:00, Sat 21:00-23:00 and Mon 20:00-22:00 [E2].\n- For BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01, BZ_P_VITTORIA and BZ_BOEHLER_01, expect user impact at any time. Consider working on one point at a time, or notifying users in advance [E3, E4].\n- Before committing, check the early-morning pattern at each specific site, since site-level data is thin [E4].\n\n## Limitations & unknowns\n- Occupancy is not demand, energy, sessions or faults, so a quiet window does not show that no one wants to charge.\n- 44 grid cells in the Bolzano profile had fewer than 4 comparable dates. Some overnight cells are 0.0 or null (for example Mon 02:00 and Tue 02:00-04:00 are null), so overnight values are weak evidence [E2].\n- Coverage is low at the top sites: BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01 is 0.147, BZ_P_VITTORIA 0.082 and BZ_BOEHLER_01 0.227, with 437, 757 and 196 gaps over 120 minutes respectively. None are stale [E3, E5].\n- For BZ_C_RISPARMIO_01, 65 grid cells had fewer than 4 comparable dates, so its site-level windows are tentative [E4].\n- 22 sites were excluded from the ranking for under 24 hours of exposure, and only 43 of 51 sites have data in the window [E1, E3].\n\n## Sources\n- [E1] dataset_overview — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14\n- [E2] hourly_profile(scope=bolzano) — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14\n- [E3] rank_sites(metric=occupancy) — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14\n- [E4] hourly_profile(scope=Neogy-AMPECO:78226) — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14\n- [E5] data_quality(site_ids=top 3 sites) — Open Data Hub South Tyrol EChargingPlug status, window 2026-09-19..2026-11-14",
